Updates in Magic Variables
Magic variables are special variables automatically available during playbook execution. In Ansible 2.20.x, they are stricter and more informative:
- ansible_playbook_python → Path to the Python interpreter running the playbook.
- ansible_playbook_path → Absolute path of the current playbook.
- ansible_failed_task → Captures the last failed task for debugging.
- ansible_run_tags → Shows which tags were applied during execution.
- ansible_check_mode → Indicates if playbook is running in --check (dry-run).


- name: Debug magic variables
  debug:
    msg: >
      Playbook path: {{ ansible_playbook_path }}
      Python used: {{ ansible_playbook_python }}
      Tags applied: {{ ansible_run_tags }}
